1
00:00:00,850 --> 00:00:05,201
The brush clears the stepped tower of a southern temple, rising in tiers.

2
00:00:05,201 --> 00:00:10,706
It was built by the Cholas, who ruled the Kaveri delta, and later sent a fleet across the sea.

3
00:00:10,706 --> 00:00:14,257
Why would a king send ships across the sea?

4
00:00:31,017 --> 00:00:39,283
How do we know? Chola inscriptions are carved on temple walls, and the Tiruvalangadu copper plates record Rajendra's victories.

5
00:00:39,283 --> 00:00:46,067
Archaeologists dug up Chola sites. Few other early dynasties left such rich records.

6
00:01:01,317 --> 00:01:09,194
The Imperial Cholas rose about 850 CE, when Vijayalaya took Thanjavur. His successors made it a base.

7
00:01:09,194 --> 00:01:15,894
Parantaka the First, about 907 to 955 CE, ruled much of the Tamil country.

8
00:01:15,894 --> 00:01:22,152
Rajaraja the First, from 985 to 1014 CE, was the first great emperor.

9
00:01:22,152 --> 00:01:30,267
He added the north of Sri Lanka and the Maldives, and built the Brihadeeswara temple at Thanjavur, completed about 1010 CE.

10
00:01:30,267 --> 00:01:39,444
His son Rajendra the First, 1014 to 1044 CE, marched to the Ganga and founded a new capital, Gangaikondacholapuram.

11
00:01:39,444 --> 00:01:46,277
In 1025 CE, Rajendra sent a naval expedition against Srivijaya, in south-east Asia.

12
00:01:46,277 --> 00:01:50,968
It was among the few times an Indian fleet projected power across the sea.

13
00:01:50,968 --> 00:01:55,072
Chola trade ties with China and south-east Asia were strong.

14
00:01:55,072 --> 00:02:02,216
After Kulottunga, the dynasty weakened and ended about 1279 CE under the Pandyas.

15
00:02:17,483 --> 00:02:27,009
Old name, new name. The Chola capital Thanjavur was written as Tanjore in colonial times. Today the official name is Thanjavur.

16
00:02:27,009 --> 00:02:31,150
The Brihadeeswara temple there is a World Heritage Site.

17
00:02:46,417 --> 00:02:56,694
Carve this tip into memory. Rajaraja: Thanjavur temple;. Rajendra: Ganga and sea. Father and son, a temple and a fleet.

18
00:02:56,694 --> 00:03:00,116
That covers the golden age of the Cholas.

19
00:03:15,383 --> 00:03:31,352
Dig Quiz. Pause and name it. Number one. Which Chola emperor built the Brihadeeswara temple? The answer: Rajaraja the First.

20
00:03:31,352 --> 00:03:45,240
Number two. Against which kingdom did Rajendra send a fleet in 1025? The answer: Srivijaya. Number three.

21
00:03:45,240 --> 00:03:57,260
What was Rajendra’s new capital? The answer: Gangaikondacholapuram. Now one line for Mains.

22
00:03:57,260 --> 00:04:02,146
Evaluate the achievements of Rajaraja the First and Rajendra the First.

23
00:04:21,417 --> 00:04:29,197
The temple tower goes into its case. It stands for the greatest of the Chola monuments. Three facts to take away.

24
00:04:29,197 --> 00:04:38,762
A tiered tower of the Chola temple. Brihadeeswara, about 1010 CE. Rajendra’s fleet sailed in 1025.

25
00:04:38,762 --> 00:04:42,638
Next gallery: Chola Village and Temple.

